les of Etna Creek with 80 acres of floodplain to create drought r", 2], ["This project proposes to accelerate mountain meadow restoration and advance conservation actions identified in the Conservation Agreement for the Eagle Lake Rainbow Trout, (CDFW et al, 2015).  Plannin", 2], ["Boney Flat is a 10-acre meadow within the 257,000 acre Rim Fire (2013) footprint. The project is a largely dry meadow, with a large (~2 acres) degrading fen, towards the bottom of the meadow. The char", 2], ["The Redwood Creek Flood Control Project leveed the lower 3.4 miles of Redwood Creek. Estuarine habitat, floodplain connectivity, riparian vegetation, and geomorphic processes were impacted. The purpos", 2], ["Beaver Haven is a property encompassing 800 ft of Sugar Creek, a key Coho spawning and rearing tributary in the Scott Watershed.  The property is ecologically vibrant with a multi-threaded channel, de", 2], ["The Project will remove the first major fish passage barrier on Santa Anita Creek situated along the Gaviota Coast, in Santa Barbara County. The proposed project includes the removal of an undersized ", 2], ["Compile existing and collect new data required to evaluate the feasibility of providing volitional passage of Nur (Chinook salmon) above Shasta Dam in support of the Winnemem Wintu Tribe?s vision of r", 2]], "date_fmt": null}, "DESC_SHORT": {"type": "TEXT", "distinct": 253, "blank": 130, "top": [["This project seeks to promote water conservation and alternative water sourcing in the upper tributaries of Green Valley Creek's Atascadero subwatershed through community outreach, site assessment, an", 2], ["This project will identify and design up to five implementation projects focused on restoring, protecting, and enhancing forest and stream health in the watershed in the Standley Creek watershed. ", 2], ["The purpose of this project is to strategically install large wood in at least 10 miles of high-priority Coho Salmon and Steelhead Trout habitat in stream reaches within Mendocino County. ", 2], ["Specific objectives of this Project are to restore and enhance riparian, instream, floodplain and side-channel habitat in Bull Creek, for the benefit of Coho Salmon. ", 2], ["This Sproul Creek Road Erosion and Fish Passage Barrier Assessment Project will result in the inventory and assessment of current and potential erosion sources and road crossing fish barriers along ap", 2], ["The project will reach out to ~57 high-priority riparian parcels identified for coho salmon recovery within the Mill Creek watershed to develop an Opportunities and Constraints Summary including multi", 2], ["The Yale Creek Salmonid Habitat Enhancement project enhances instream spawning habitat for Coho and steelhead by installing selected large woody debris (LWD) habitat enhancement structures and impleme", 2], ["The primary goal of this planning project will be to survey the mainstem Eel River and South Fork Eel River, identify any patches of Arundo, collect location and descriptive data of the patches, and d", 2], ["This Project is Phase II of the overall restoration of Hester Marsh in Elkhorn Slough and shall restore 30 acres of historically diked and drained coastal wetlands and five acres adjacent vegetated bu", 2], ["This Project will support the restoration of 2,655 acres of mountain meadow in Red Clover Valley.", 2], ["Will restore the Van Norden meadow, approximately 485 acres of meadow habitat. Will restore function to the stream and meadow ecosystem of the headwaters of the South Yuba River. ", 2]], "date_fmt": null}, "NUMBER": {"type": "TEXT", "distinct": 376, "blank": 0, "top": [["1729752", 3], ["1730552", 3], ["Q2196507", 3], ["1730617", 2], ["1730452", 2], ["1729278", 2], ["1730072", 2], ["1730947", 2], ["1730740", 2], ["1731130", 2], ["1730020", 2], ["1729633", 2]], "date_fmt": null}, "AWARD": {"type": "TEXT", "distinct": 366, "blank": 0, "top": [["$1,000,000", 5], ["$1,500,000", 4], ["$500,000", 4], ["$787,250", 3], ["$5,000,000", 3], ["$4,000